## Non-diagonal source removal and the actual chronological target

If no physical source-removal evolution is claimed, a directly supplied post-delivery B diagonal satisfying the theorem's event bound is sufficient for compression. For the actual non-diagonal quench considered here, the stronger premise is

    rho_B=tau_G,

or a supplied full reduced trace-distance allowance (1/2)||rho_B-tau_G||_1<=d. The initial joint rho_ZB may have arbitrary coherences and arbitrary old/reference correlations. It is not required to factorize. With disjoint K_Z and a nonnegative regular nonincreasing envelope u_q from 1 to 0,

    U_q=exp(-it_q K_Z) tensor exp(-i A_q G),
    A_q=integral_0^t_q u_q(t)dt,
    rho_q=U_q rho_ZB U_q*.

The full reduced Gibbs density commutes with G, so its marginal remains tau_G. Correlations in rho_q can change. An approximate reduced-state promise remains at distance d under the ideal switch and hence changes every specified computational event by at most d. Use delta_bar=min(1,s t_r+d) in g. This is an event-TV allowance used once; it does not make the approximate input satisfy every rare full conditional. It also supplies no approximation of the whole joint input to a product state.

The preparation then uses the parent's positive compensation C=kappa I-F_inst, assembled from actual positive local blocks, B_F>=||F_inst|| and B_C>=||C||. The complete nominal preparation generator is

    H_p(t)=H0+(1-u_p(t))F_inst+u_p(t)kappa I+G_p(t).

The installed K_Z must itself have the supplied positivity/reserve property. All gates run on the fully compensated plateau. Every pulse, both ramps and every guard contribute to the actual elapsed T_p. On the ideal comparator the completed record-transfer/synthesis map has the parent's phase exp[-i(kappa A_u+Theta)] and H0 aging for that whole T_p. The target applies the actual K_Z evolution for t_q first, then the H0-aged preparation map, to the complete rho_q/sigma_c construction. These generally cannot be collapsed to one exponential because K_Z and H0 need not commute. The source phase exp(-i a_TF A_q) and all nonconstant source phases remain in the propagator and ledger.

The comparison order is full-space turn-on, the single pure-comparator replacement, and only then the ready-range release estimate Gamma>=||F_inst J_ready|| on the whole retained complement. With the parent's actual ramp durations r_on,r_off and full-space implementation residuals E_q,E_p, the sufficient final unhalved trace price is

    min(2, g(delta_bar)+B_F r_on+Gamma r_off
           +2 integral||E_q(t)||dt+2 integral||E_p(t)||dt).

A separately supplied full-input comparison error adds once if a fixed different target is used. No actual faulty state is assumed ready for the restricted release bound. Omega is the exact modeled complement; replacing it by the actual faulty midpoint marginal needs its own marginal-change allowance. The finite clock release Gram/covariance calculations and the full-sector norms remain those of the unchanged parent consumer.

Every interval counted solely as H0 aging must have u_p=1 throughout. An uncompensated wait must appear as its actual ordered segment in the target or contribute its comparison residual. Its elapsed time cannot be dropped because its nominal and actual idle controls happen to agree. Compensation action is exactly ||C||A_u and **at most** B_C A_u. The thermal field must vanish at the declared endpoint; otherwise the changed installed baseline, positivity, release, scalar and moment accounts must be recomputed. Integrated norm errors alone do not guarantee positivity or bound endpoint energy, bandwidth or work.

## Source scalar, channel, time and work ledger

For the literal positive blocks the whole-space norm allowance and independently calibrated uncollected Pauli-channel load are

    kappa_TF=sum_i(h_i+2g_i)+sum_e[c_e+max(J_e,0)]+k0,
    ||G||<=kappa_TF,
    S_unc=sum_i[h_i+g_i+|a_i|+|b_i|]
          +sum_e[|c_e+J_e/4|+3|J_e|/4]+k0.

The full Pauli identity coefficient and fully collected operator coefficient sum are

    a_TF=(1/2)sum_i h_i+sum_i g_i+sum_e(c_e+J_e/4)+k0,
    S_col=|a_TF|+sum_i|h_i/2+(1/4)sum_(e incident i)J_e|
          +(1/4)sum_e|J_e|+sum_i(|a_i|+|b_i|).

Under the stated margin and reserve hypotheses,

    S_unc-S_col=sum_e max(0,-J_e).

The root ledger charges S_unc for its supplied independent channels; the independent proof's S_col describes a separately collected operator implementation. Attractive-edge cancellations cannot lower independent channel calibration costs silently. The source-phase gauge used in a probability proof cannot replace actual |a_i|+|b_i| hardware costs by g_i. The scalar removed there is C_block=k0+sum_e c_e+sum_i g_i, which is different from a_TF. Neither can be dropped from physical phases or energy accounting.

A robust constant transverse reserve t_i>=g_i adds sum_i(t_i-g_i) to G, its scalar, norm allowance and channel load. It leaves tau_G and its computational probabilities unchanged while changing physical phase and work. Bounded degree and uniformly bounded h_i,J_e,c_e,g_i with k0=O(L) imply kappa_TF,S_unc=O(L). Action and slew additionally require bounded A_q and ||u_q'||_infinity. A bound on A_q does not bound t_q or eliminate old-system aging.

For a regular monotone source profile with endpoints 1 and 0, the source-field action, peak, slew and total variation are respectively A_q||G||, ||G||, ||u_q'||_infinity||G|| and ||G||. A finite slew requires the stated regularity and derivative bound. These are source-field costs; old-generator, compensation, gate, isolation and all elapsed-time costs are additional. The complete inherited literal positive gate, scalar and channel budgets remain required. An operator-norm bound on the total generator is not interchangeable with separately positive physical channels.

The ideal source expectation is conserved for any input because G commutes with K_Z+u_qG. Thus its formal switch work is W_q=-Tr(G rho_B(0)). Stationarity of the entire B marginal is a separate use of the full-density premise. The process starts with K_Z+G and ends with K_Z; this is not a same-Hamiltonian cycle, a free supply or a recycling certificate. Fault work must be compared using actual endpoint Hamiltonian/norm contracts or the appropriate variation/trajectory contracts. A time-integrated state-error allowance alone gives no absolute endpoint work price.

For bounded retained moments, centered and raw quantities stay distinct. If K=aI+K_tilde, a centered m-th power has the ordinary norm-duality allowance ||K_tilde||^m times the full trace error. A raw m-th power requires its full binomial scalar and lower-moment terms, including a^m times any difference of the retained marginal. General operator-valued partial traces and noncommuting retained tests use the parent's general trace-norm/operator-norm duality; they are not automatically real covariances. Old/control covariance, reference records, full source scalars and the actual baseline are retained. No small centered moment claim erases a large scalar energy or a changed marginal.

For fixed finite s and strict computable q_bar<1/2, the majority recurrence tends to zero and some finite r reaches any specified event budget. Arbitrary readiness accuracy additionally requires d and every implementation/ramp/isolation allowance to improve accordingly. A fixed delivery error floor or a growing unpriced lifetime residual is not removed by increasing L. No common hardware cap, efficient thermal sampler, native switch, native controller or thermodynamic preparation cost is proved.

## Retained witnesses, exposure and evidence limits

The narrow witnesses are part of the scope, not a broad no-go claim.

- Small global event-TV does not preserve rare full conditionals. For independent g=0 Gibbs bits with p0<1/2, shift mass (1-p0)p0^(L-1) from x_i=0 to x_i=1 at the all-one complement record. The complement marginal is unchanged and total variation is arbitrarily small as L grows, but that conditional becomes 1. This explains the single additive bad-event allowance.
- A retained reference can copy the computational record. Reference-conditioned bits may then be certain although the B marginal obeys the theorem. All records remain and no reference-conditioned q_bar is asserted.
- A matching diagonal is insufficient before the non-diagonal quench. For G=h n+gI-gX, h,g>0, let R=sqrt(h^2+4g^2), z=(h/R)tanh(beta R/2), and rho=(I+yY+zZ)/2 with 0<y<sqrt(1-z^2). It has tau_G's diagonal, but d Tr(n exp(-iAG)rho exp(iAG))/dA at A=0 is gy>0.
- The positive transverse-pair example h(n_1+n_2)+epsilon(I-X_1X_2) can have a rare conditional near 1. Its pair flip is outside the onsite class and destroys the specific one-site path factorization. Its scalar reserve is kept; no generic noncommuting extension is claimed.
- The consumer's uncompensated-wait, normalized-success and faulty-midpoint retargeting witnesses remain applicable. A loose B_C bound is not an exact action. An actual unused factor is not certified pure by a comparison-state replacement.

